('127.476.d.4.C',4,'Professional societies and university programs help students learn about careers and about:','["sports scores", "training requirements", "fashion trends", "bus routes"]'::jsonb,1,'They explain how to enter fields.','original'),
('127.476.d.5.A',3,'A person who analyzes DNA sequence data with computers has a career in:','["aviation", "retail", "bioinformatics", "carpentry"]'::jsonb,2,'Bioinformatics analyzes sequences.','original'),
('127.476.d.5.A',4,'A genetic counselor helps families understand the risk of inherited:','["debts", "holidays", "fashions", "conditions"]'::jsonb,3,'Counselors explain genetic risks.','original'),
('127.476.d.5.B',3,'A recent advance such as rapid DNA sequencing is significant because it can find genetic differences quickly and at a lower:','["cost", "color", "height", "weight"]'::jsonb,0,'Sequencing has become cheaper.','original'),
('127.476.d.5.B',4,'Advances in forensic science, such as DNA databases, help solve crimes by connecting evidence to:','["buildings", "individuals", "clouds", "days of the week"]'::jsonb,1,'Databases link evidence to people.','original'),
('127.476.d.5.C',3,'One bioethical issue in biotechnology is whether people''s genetic information should be kept:','["loud", "forgotten", "private", "public by default"]'::jsonb,2,'Genetic privacy matters.','original'),
('127.476.d.5.C',4,'Editing genes in human embryos raises bioethical concerns about safety, fairness, and long-term:','["fashion", "prices of paper", "weather", "consequences"]'::jsonb,3,'Embryo editing affects future generations.','original'),
('127.476.d.5.D',3,'A job-specific resume for a laboratory technician should highlight lab skills, education, and:','["relevant experience", "nicknames", "pets", "favorite foods"]'::jsonb,0,'Resumes match the job.','original'),
('127.476.d.5.D',4,'When applying for a quality control position, the resume should list skills such as documentation and:','["singing", "accurate measurement", "drawing cartoons", "juggling"]'::jsonb,1,'Skills should fit the job.','original'),
('127.476.d.5.E',3,'A career plan lists goals, the education needed, and the steps and:','["bills", "nicknames", "timeline", "colors"]'::jsonb,2,'Plans have steps and times.','original'),
('127.476.d.5.E',4,'Updating a career plan each year is wise because goals, skills, and the job market can:','["vanish forever", "freeze", "stay identical", "change"]'::jsonb,3,'Plans must be revised.','original'),
('127.476.d.6.A',3,'Identifying whether a study is an experiment, a survey, or an observation means identifying its scientific:','["methodology", "poster", "cover", "budget"]'::jsonb,0,'Methodology describes the approach.','original'),
('127.476.d.6.A',4,'A researcher who compares a treated group with an untreated group is using a:','["guess", "controlled experiment", "novel", "poem"]'::jsonb,1,'Controls and treatment form an experiment.','original'),
('127.476.d.6.B',3,'In an experiment testing how light affects plant growth, the amount of light is the:','["constant", "control group", "independent variable", "dependent variable"]'::jsonb,2,'The tested factor is independent.','original'),
('127.476.d.6.B',4,'In the same experiment, the height of the plants that is measured is the:','["hypothesis", "independent variable", "control", "dependent variable"]'::jsonb,3,'The measured result is dependent.','original'),
('127.476.d.6.C',3,'Reading a protocol closely helps a technician understand the purpose of each:','["step", "font", "footer", "page color"]'::jsonb,0,'Each step has a reason.','original'),
('127.476.d.6.C',4,'A protocol step says to keep a sample on ice. The purpose is most likely to prevent the sample from:','["evaporating into steel", "degrading", "growing hair", "glowing"]'::jsonb,1,'Cold slows degradation.','original'),
('127.476.d.6.D',3,'Deciding whether a conclusion is supported by the results means you should:','["change the numbers", "skip the methods", "interpret the data", "ignore the graph"]'::jsonb,2,'Conclusions follow from data.','original'),
('127.476.d.6.D',4,'A conclusion says a drug works, but the control group improved just as much. The conclusion is:','["proven", "unrelated to controls", "strongly supported", "not supported by the data"]'::jsonb,3,'Controls show no extra effect.','original'),
('127.476.d.7.A',3,'Before running an assay, scientists define its requirements, such as how sensitive and how specific it must be. This is part of:','["assay design", "car design", "poster design", "menu design"]'::jsonb,0,'Assays are designed to meet needs.','original'),
('127.476.d.7.A',4,'Optimizing an assay means adjusting conditions such as temperature and reagent amounts to get the best:','["smell", "signal", "handwriting", "taste"]'::jsonb,1,'Optimization improves performance.','original'),
('127.476.d.7.B',3,'A statistical test used to see if the difference between two groups is likely real rather than due to chance is the:','["time test", "tone test", "t-test", "tea test"]'::jsonb,2,'The t-test compares means.','original'),
('127.476.d.7.B',4,'A p-value below 0.05 usually means the result is unlikely to be due to:','["the laboratory", "the sample label", "measurement units", "chance alone"]'::jsonb,3,'Low p suggests significance.','original'),
('127.476.d.7.C',3,'To find the concentration of an unknown protein, a scientist graphs known standards and reads the unknown''s value from the standard:','["curve", "clock", "label", "menu"]'::jsonb,0,'Standard curves convert signal to concentration.','original'),
('127.476.d.7.C',4,'On a standard curve, the unknown protein sample''s absorbance is compared with those of the known:','["strangers", "standards", "guesses", "fabrics"]'::jsonb,1,'Knowns calibrate the curve.','original'),
('127.476.d.7.D',3,'Enzyme kinetics studies how fast an enzyme converts its substrate into a:','["machine", "chapter", "product", "picture"]'::jsonb,2,'Enzymes make products.','original'),
('127.476.d.7.D',4,'In a colorimetric assay, a color change that is measured over time shows the reaction:','["name", "owner", "volume", "rate"]'::jsonb,3,'Color change tracks rate.','original'),
('127.476.d.8.A',3,'In recombinant DNA technology, a gene is inserted into a vector, which then delivers it into a:','["host cell", "pencil case", "shoe box", "bottle cap"]'::jsonb,0,'Hosts express the gene.','original'),
('127.476.d.8.A',4,'After the vector is put into host cells, the cells that took it up can be found because the vector carries a:','["receipt", "selectable marker", "window", "birthday"]'::jsonb,1,'Markers identify transformed cells.','original'),
('127.476.d.8.B',3,'Green fluorescent protein is useful in biotechnology because it glows under:','["magnets", "salt water", "ultraviolet light", "sound"]'::jsonb,2,'GFP fluoresces under UV.','original'),
('127.476.d.8.B',4,'Bacteria that have taken up a GFP gene will glow green, showing that the gene was successfully:','["frozen", "deleted", "bought", "expressed"]'::jsonb,3,'Glowing proves expression.','original'),
('127.476.d.8.C',3,'The technique ELISA uses antibodies to detect and measure a:','["specific protein", "rock type", "cloud shape", "coin"]'::jsonb,0,'ELISA detects proteins.','original'),
('127.476.d.8.C',4,'A pregnancy test and some disease tests use an antibody-based method similar to:','["tuning", "ELISA", "welding", "carving"]'::jsonb,1,'Antibody detection is the principle.','original'),
('127.476.d.8.D',3,'A technique that separates proteins by their charge or size while moving through a gel is protein:','["fishing", "printing", "electrophoresis", "painting"]'::jsonb,2,'Gels separate proteins.','original'),
('127.476.d.8.D',4,'Column chromatography can purify a protein by letting the mixture flow through beads that bind the protein of interest, which is called:','["random sorting", "paper folding", "dry cleaning", "affinity purification"]'::jsonb,3,'Affinity beads capture targets.','original'),
('127.476.d.9.A',3,'Plant cells grown in a culture dish with nutrients and hormones can develop into new:','["plants", "rocks", "songs", "engines"]'::jsonb,0,'Plant tissue is totipotent.','original'),
('127.476.d.9.A',4,'A tissue culture lab must prevent fungal contamination by using sterile media and:','["open windows", "aseptic technique", "dark paint", "dirty tools"]'::jsonb,1,'Aseptic work keeps cultures clean.','original'),
('127.476.d.9.B',3,'Changing the pH of a medium too far from optimum can cause cells to grow:','["into metal", "faster forever", "poorly", "perfectly"]'::jsonb,2,'Growth depends on proper conditions.','original'),
('127.476.d.9.B',4,'To study the effect of temperature on cell growth, a scientist grows cultures at several temperatures and compares their:','["bottle sizes", "names", "labels", "growth rates"]'::jsonb,3,'Compare outcomes across conditions.','original'),
('127.476.d.9.C',3,'After bacteria are transformed with a plasmid, the plasmid can be checked by cutting it with a restriction enzyme and looking at the:','["fragment pattern", "room size", "bottle shape", "label color"]'::jsonb,0,'Digest patterns confirm the plasmid.','original'),
