('127.476.d.9.D',3,'Plasmids replicate easily in bacteria, whereas viral vectors are especially good at delivering genes into:','["rocks", "glass", "animal cells", "metal"]'::jsonb,2,'Viral vectors infect cells efficiently.','original'),
('127.476.d.9.D',4,'One reason scientists choose a viral vector over a plasmid for gene therapy is that viruses naturally enter:','["soil", "paper", "batteries", "human cells"]'::jsonb,3,'Viruses are good at entering cells.','original'),
