('127.478.d.8.B',3,'A student on a clinical rotation uses the term hypertension in a chart rather than high blood pressure. This is using medical:','["jokes", "slang", "vocabulary", "rumors"]'::jsonb,2,'Vocabulary should be accurate.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.B',4,'Using the abbreviation approved by the facility rather than making one up shows that a student is employing correct:','["dress", "fashion", "timing", "terminology"]'::jsonb,3,'Facility-approved terms prevent errors.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.C',3,'In a simulated setting, admitting a patient includes checking identification, taking vital signs, and recording a:','["medical history", "dress code", "game score", "food review"]'::jsonb,0,'Admission gathers history.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.C',4,'Before a patient is discharged, the worker reviews written instructions and makes sure the patient understands them, called discharge:','["billing", "teaching", "punishment", "parking"]'::jsonb,1,'Discharge teaching supports recovery.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.D',3,'Helping a patient bathe, dress, and eat are examples of assisting with activities of:','["sports", "the weekend", "daily living", "art"]'::jsonb,2,'ADLs are basic self-care tasks.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.D',4,'When helping a patient with eating, bathing, and dressing, a health worker should encourage the patient to do what they can to maintain:','["anger", "boredom", "dependency", "independence"]'::jsonb,3,'Independence aids recovery.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.E',3,'A patient who has trouble balancing while walking may need a gait belt and a walker or:','["a cane", "a bicycle", "high heels", "roller skates"]'::jsonb,0,'Assistive devices support walking.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.E',4,'A gait belt placed around a patient''s waist helps the health worker support the patient during:','["sleep", "ambulation", "reading", "eating"]'::jsonb,1,'Gait belts assist walking.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.F',3,'Gently moving a patient''s joint through its normal movement to maintain flexibility is called:','["range of travel", "range of hearing", "range of motion", "range of vision"]'::jsonb,2,'ROM exercises move joints.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.F',4,'Active range of motion exercises are done by the patient on their own, while in passive exercises the:','["patient sleeps", "joint is removed", "patient runs", "worker moves the joint"]'::jsonb,3,'Passive ROM is done by someone else.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.G',3,'When a patient is upset and shouting, a good first response is to stay calm and:','["listen", "walk away", "laugh", "shout back"]'::jsonb,0,'De-escalate by listening.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.G',4,'In a role play of an emergency, remaining calm, speaking clearly, and following the plan helps manage:','["decor", "stress", "profit", "traffic"]'::jsonb,1,'Staying calm is crucial.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.H',3,'The first step for a person who is not responding and not breathing normally is to check for responsiveness and call for:','["a pencil", "a snack", "help", "a mirror"]'::jsonb,2,'Call for help quickly.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.H',4,'Adult CPR compressions should be given at a rate of about:','["50 to 60 per minute", "20 to 30 per minute", "200 to 250 per minute", "100 to 120 per minute"]'::jsonb,3,'Guideline rate for adults.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.I',3,'Taking a patient''s temperature, pulse, and blood pressure are basic skills for many health professionals. They are called:','["vital signs", "vital lists", "vital forms", "vital pages"]'::jsonb,0,'Vital signs track health.','original'),
('127.478.d.8.I',4,'Skills such as measuring pulse and respiration are used in many health science careers, so they are considered:','["rare", "basic skills", "advanced only", "unneeded"]'::jsonb,1,'Basic skills are widely used.','original'),
('127.478.d.9.A',3,'The American Nurses Association and the American Medical Association are professional:','["banks", "stores", "associations", "airlines"]'::jsonb,2,'Associations set standards.','original'),
('127.478.d.9.A',4,'State boards of nursing and medicine are regulatory agencies that license professionals and protect the:','["weather", "lunch", "board members only", "public"]'::jsonb,3,'Regulation protects the public.','original'),
('127.478.d.9.B',3,'A document that states patients'' rights to respect, privacy, and informed decisions is the Patient:','["Bill of Rights", "Price List", "Parking Plan", "Seating Chart"]'::jsonb,0,'The Patient Bill of Rights.','original'),
('127.478.d.9.B',4,'Informed consent means a patient agrees to treatment after being told the benefits, risks, and:','["costs of lunch", "alternatives", "weather", "hours of sunlight"]'::jsonb,1,'Consent requires information.','original'),
('127.478.d.9.C',3,'Practicing outside one''s training or sharing patient information without permission can lead to legal consequences such as loss of:','["umbrella", "keys", "license", "lunch"]'::jsonb,2,'Misconduct risks licensure.','original'),
('127.478.d.9.C',4,'A health worker who neglects a patient may be found guilty of:','["punctuality", "courtesy", "tardiness only", "negligence"]'::jsonb,3,'Negligence is failure to give proper care.','original'),
('127.478.d.10.A',3,'A leader in health care listens, communicates clearly, takes responsibility, and shows:','["integrity", "pride only", "laziness", "secrecy"]'::jsonb,0,'Leaders show integrity.','original'),
('127.478.d.10.A',4,'A health science leader inspires teamwork by setting a good example and giving credit to others, which builds:','["gossip", "trust", "delays", "fear"]'::jsonb,1,'Leaders build trust.','original'),
('127.478.d.10.B',3,'Observing how team members interact, who leads, and who is quiet is assessing group:','["weights", "colors", "dynamics", "heights"]'::jsonb,2,'Group dynamics are patterns of interaction.','original'),
('127.478.d.10.B',4,'A team has two members who always dominate while others are silent. A leader who notices this has assessed group:','["budgets", "menus", "supplies", "dynamics"]'::jsonb,3,'Dynamics affect outcomes.','original'),
('127.478.d.10.C',3,'A method for helping a group reach agreement that all can support is building:','["consensus", "competition", "confusion", "conflict"]'::jsonb,0,'Consensus involves everyone.','original'),
('127.478.d.10.C',4,'To integrate consensus-building, a leader invites each person to share, summarizes common ground, and checks that everyone can:','["avoid work", "accept the decision", "leave early", "disagree silently"]'::jsonb,1,'Consensus means broad acceptance.','original'),
('127.478.d.11.A',3,'Workplace safety rules in the United States are enforced by an agency called:','["NASA", "IRS", "OSHA", "FBI"]'::jsonb,2,'OSHA protects workers.','original'),
('127.478.d.11.A',4,'The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention issues guidelines on infection control that health facilities follow to protect:','["only managers", "only vendors", "only visitors", "patients and workers"]'::jsonb,3,'CDC guidelines protect everyone.','original'),
('127.478.d.11.B',3,'Chemicals, medical waste, and blood spills are examples of hazardous materials that require:','["special handling", "ordinary trash", "bare hands", "no care"]'::jsonb,0,'Hazards require proper procedures.','original'),
('127.478.d.11.B',4,'A biohazard bag, usually red or marked with a symbol, is used to dispose of items contaminated with:','["food scraps only", "blood or body fluids", "clean linens", "paper"]'::jsonb,1,'Biohazard waste is separated.','original'),
('127.478.d.11.C',3,'A worker who sees a wet floor in a hallway should report the unsafe condition and put up a:','["decoration", "plant", "warning sign", "curtain"]'::jsonb,2,'Mark hazards and report them.','original'),
('127.478.d.11.C',4,'Reporting an unsafe condition promptly helps prevent:','["discounts", "vacations", "promotions", "injuries"]'::jsonb,3,'Reporting protects people.','original'),
('127.478.d.11.D',3,'Sorting waste and recycling paper and plastics in a hospital helps lower costs and protect the:','["environment", "front desk", "parking lot", "uniform"]'::jsonb,0,'Recycling helps cost containment.','original'),
('127.478.d.11.D',4,'Reusing supplies safely and sorting waste correctly are ways a facility practices cost:','["growth", "containment", "inflation", "debt"]'::jsonb,1,'Waste management saves money.','original'),
('127.478.d.11.E',3,'To lift a heavy object safely, a health worker should bend at the knees, keep the back straight, and keep the load:','["high above the head", "far from the body", "close to the body", "behind the back"]'::jsonb,2,'Proper body mechanics prevent injury.','original'),
('127.478.d.11.E',4,'Proper body mechanics when moving a patient reduce the worker''s risk of a back:','["promotion", "bonus", "vacation", "injury"]'::jsonb,3,'Proper technique prevents injury.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.A',3,'Eating well, exercising, and getting vaccines are wellness strategies for the:','["prevention of disease", "spread of disease", "increase of disease", "cause of disease"]'::jsonb,0,'Prevention keeps people healthy.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.A',4,'Handwashing and regular screenings help prevent disease by catching or stopping problems:','["late", "early", "never", "randomly"]'::jsonb,1,'Early action prevents illness.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.B',3,'Supportive friends and family can improve physical and mental health, while toxic relationships can increase:','["energy", "sleep", "stress", "rest"]'::jsonb,2,'Relationships affect health.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.B',4,'A person in a harmful relationship might experience anxiety and sleep problems, which are negative effects on mental and physical:','["fashion", "travel", "wealth", "health"]'::jsonb,3,'Relationships can harm health.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.C',3,'When community members support each other through volunteering and neighborhood programs, health outcomes tend to:','["improve", "worsen", "stop", "vanish"]'::jsonb,0,'Social bonds improve health.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.C',4,'Community health fairs and support groups show the benefits of positive relationships between members and local:','["traffic lights", "health resources", "stadiums", "billboards"]'::jsonb,1,'Community connection promotes wellness.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.D',3,'People without insurance or nearby clinics may have difficulty getting care, a problem of access to quality:','["music", "tickets", "health care", "fashion"]'::jsonb,2,'Access affects outcomes.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.D',4,'Long travel distances and high costs are barriers that reduce a person''s access to:','["tourism", "leisure", "sports", "medical services"]'::jsonb,3,'Barriers limit care.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.E',3,'Acupuncture and massage are examples of alternative health practices called complementary or alternative:','["therapies", "diseases", "plans", "tests"]'::jsonb,0,'These are therapies.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.E',4,'Before trying an alternative therapy, patients should talk to a provider and check whether it is supported by:','["popular opinion", "scientific evidence", "advertisements", "rumors"]'::jsonb,1,'Evidence matters.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.F',3,'After a serious injury, the structure and function of the body can change, such as a broken bone that limits:','["temperature", "eyesight color", "movement", "hair length"]'::jsonb,2,'Trauma changes function.','original'),
('127.478.d.12.F',4,'Diseases such as arthritis change the structure of joints and reduce their:','["names", "numbers", "colors", "function"]'::jsonb,3,'Disease alters structure and function.','original'),
('127.479.d.1.A',3,'A nurse must give 3 doses of 125 mg each. The total amount in milligrams is:','["375", "250", "128", "500"]'::jsonb,0,'3 x 125 = 375.','original'),
