('127.479.d.8.I',3,'A medical assistant who measures a patient''s height and weight is performing a skill specific to a health science:','["pilot", "traveler", "professional", "chef"]'::jsonb,2,'Skills fit the profession.','original'),
('127.479.d.8.I',4,'A phlebotomist''s key skill is drawing blood with a needle, a skill specific to that:','["sport", "game", "hobby", "profession"]'::jsonb,3,'Skills are job specific.','original'),
('127.479.d.9.A',3,'An organization such as the American Red Cross is a:','["professional or service association", "farm", "airline", "bank"]'::jsonb,0,'Associations support the field.','original'),
('127.479.d.9.A',4,'State boards that license health workers are examples of:','["hotels", "regulatory agencies", "fan clubs", "stores"]'::jsonb,1,'Regulators enforce standards.','original'),
('127.479.d.9.B',3,'Legal and ethical standards in health care include protecting patient:','["advertising", "parking", "confidentiality", "decor"]'::jsonb,2,'Confidentiality is a core duty.','original'),
('127.479.d.9.B',4,'The Patient Bill of Rights says patients have the right to considerate care and to make decisions about their:','["uniform", "parking", "phone plan", "treatment"]'::jsonb,3,'Rights include decision-making.','original'),
('127.479.d.9.C',3,'A worker who shares a patient''s medical information on social media may face dismissal and legal action for violating:','["privacy laws", "dress codes", "seating plans", "parking rules"]'::jsonb,0,'Privacy breaches have penalties.','original'),
('127.479.d.9.C',4,'Unacceptable behavior such as theft or neglect can lead to loss of a job and to legal and ethical:','["rewards", "consequences", "promotions", "holidays"]'::jsonb,1,'Misconduct has consequences.','original'),
('127.479.d.9.D',3,'A nursing assistant who performs only tasks she has been trained and allowed to do is working within her:','["scope of pay", "scope of dress", "scope of practice", "scope of travel"]'::jsonb,2,'Scope defines allowed tasks.','original'),
('127.479.d.9.D',4,'Giving a medication when only a licensed nurse is permitted to do so would go beyond a nursing assistant''s:','["uniform", "lunch break", "schedule", "scope of practice"]'::jsonb,3,'Staying in scope protects patients.','original'),
('127.479.d.10.A',3,'A good leader in health care listens, communicates clearly, and takes:','["responsibility", "breaks always", "shortcuts", "credit only"]'::jsonb,0,'Leaders take responsibility.','original'),
('127.479.d.10.A',4,'Leadership skills such as delegating tasks and encouraging coworkers help a team stay:','["silent", "organized", "separate", "confused"]'::jsonb,1,'Leaders organize.','original'),
('127.479.d.10.B',3,'Taking part in a team project by sharing ideas and respecting others is participating in group:','["weights", "accidents", "dynamics", "meals"]'::jsonb,2,'Group dynamics include participation.','original'),
('127.479.d.10.B',4,'In a group, a member who tends to take notes and keep the team on schedule has a:','["problem", "debt", "hobby", "role"]'::jsonb,3,'Groups have roles.','original'),
('127.479.d.10.C',3,'When a team uses consensus-building, the decision reflects the views of:','["all members", "the newest member", "one member only", "the loudest voice"]'::jsonb,0,'Consensus considers everyone.','original'),
('127.479.d.10.C',4,'A team that cannot agree can try consensus-building by listing the options and finding the one everyone can:','["delay", "support", "avoid", "forget"]'::jsonb,1,'Find common ground.','original'),
('127.479.d.11.A',3,'The agency that sets standards to protect workers from workplace hazards is:','["NASA", "NBA", "OSHA", "FDA"]'::jsonb,2,'OSHA protects workers.','original'),
('127.479.d.11.A',4,'Health facilities conform to national rules on preventing the spread of germs, known as infection:','["decoration", "growth", "pricing", "control"]'::jsonb,3,'CDC infection control guidelines.','original'),
('127.479.d.11.B',3,'Protocols for hazardous materials tell workers how to handle, store, and dispose of dangerous:','["substances", "charts", "menus", "colors"]'::jsonb,0,'Protocols address hazards.','original'),
('127.479.d.11.B',4,'A spill of a chemical or blood in a clinical area is handled according to protocol with proper protective equipment and:','["shouting", "cleanup procedures", "taking photos", "ignoring"]'::jsonb,1,'Follow cleanup protocol.','original'),
('127.479.d.11.C',3,'Observing a frayed cord on medical equipment and telling a supervisor is an example of reporting an:','["opinion", "rumor", "unsafe condition", "joke"]'::jsonb,2,'Observe and report hazards.','original'),
('127.479.d.11.C',4,'Unsafe conditions should be reported, along with who noticed them and the time, so the problem can be:','["repeated", "praised", "hidden", "fixed"]'::jsonb,3,'Reporting enables correction.','original'),
('127.479.d.11.D',3,'Separating recyclable paper and plastics from regular trash is part of waste management and helps the:','["environment", "cafeteria menu", "uniform", "lobby"]'::jsonb,0,'Recycling protects the environment.','original'),
('127.479.d.11.D',4,'Using supplies carefully and not wasting them is a way to practice cost:','["inflation", "containment", "debt", "growth"]'::jsonb,1,'Careful use controls costs.','original'),
('127.479.d.12.A',3,'Regular exercise, a balanced diet, and getting enough sleep are strategies for the prevention of:','["fitness", "growth", "disease", "health"]'::jsonb,2,'Wellness prevents disease.','original'),
('127.479.d.12.A',4,'Vaccines, screenings, and handwashing are strategies that help prevent the spread of:','["fitness", "comfort", "wealth", "illness"]'::jsonb,3,'Prevention stops illness.','original'),
('127.479.d.12.B',3,'Friends who encourage healthy habits have a positive effect on a person''s:','["physical and mental health", "clothes", "bank balance", "travel plans"]'::jsonb,0,'Positive relationships help health.','original'),
('127.479.d.12.B',4,'A stressful, unsupportive relationship may raise blood pressure and lower mood, an example of a negative effect on:','["looks", "health", "clothing", "wealth"]'::jsonb,1,'Stress harms health.','original'),
('127.479.d.12.C',3,'Health workers who share information with each other in a community help make care more:','["delayed", "confusing", "coordinated", "expensive"]'::jsonb,2,'Cooperation improves care.','original'),
('127.479.d.12.C',4,'Positive relationships among community health workers, such as sharing referrals, benefit the patients'' access to:','["games", "vacations", "fashion", "services"]'::jsonb,3,'Collaboration improves service.','original'),
('127.479.d.12.D',3,'People who live far from clinics or lack insurance have limited access to:','["quality health care", "quality shoes", "quality vacations", "quality music"]'::jsonb,0,'Access varies.','original'),
('127.479.d.12.D',4,'Researching how cost, distance, and language affect health care shows how these barriers limit people''s:','["vacations", "access", "hobbies", "income"]'::jsonb,1,'Barriers limit access.','original'),
('127.479.d.12.E',3,'Acupuncture, chiropractic care, and herbal remedies are examples of alternative health:','["laws", "diseases", "practices", "tests"]'::jsonb,2,'Alternatives are practices.','original'),
('127.479.d.12.E',4,'A responsible health worker researching an alternative therapy looks for evidence of both its benefits and its possible:','["colors", "prices of paper", "slogans", "risks"]'::jsonb,3,'Weigh benefits and risks.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.A',3,'Heart disease, cancer, and stroke are among the leading causes of death in developed countries. Understanding how they harm the body is studying their:','["pathophysiology", "architecture", "geography", "economics"]'::jsonb,0,'Pathophysiology is the study of how disease changes function.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.A',4,'A buildup of fatty plaque in arteries narrows them and can cause a heart attack or stroke. This condition is called:','["anemia", "atherosclerosis", "arthritis", "asthma"]'::jsonb,1,'Plaque narrows arteries.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.B',3,'The smallpox vaccine helped eliminate an illness that once killed millions, showing how medical technology changed the history of:','["fashion", "music", "disease", "cooking"]'::jsonb,2,'Vaccines changed disease history.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.B',4,'The invention of the microscope helped scientists discover germs, which led to the germ theory of:','["weather", "tides", "gravity", "disease"]'::jsonb,3,'Microscopes revealed microbes.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.C',3,'Diseases like malaria and cholera are more common in developing countries, partly because of limited access to clean water and:','["health care", "video games", "fashion", "tourism"]'::jsonb,0,'Resources affect disease burden.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.C',4,'Developed countries tend to see more chronic diseases such as diabetes and heart disease, while developing countries often face more:','["sports injuries", "infectious diseases", "fashion errors", "traffic jams"]'::jsonb,1,'Disease patterns differ.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.D',3,'The organization of the United Nations that works to improve health around the world is the World Health Organization, abbreviated:','["NASA", "OPEC", "WHO", "NATO"]'::jsonb,2,'The WHO leads global health.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.D',4,'In the United States, the agency that tracks disease outbreaks and promotes disease prevention is the Centers for Disease:','["Creation and Production", "Care and Purchase", "Cure and Promotion", "Control and Prevention"]'::jsonb,3,'CDC stands for Centers for Disease Control and Prevention.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.E',3,'The number of new cases of a disease in a population during a period of time is called its:','["incidence", "prevalence", "morbidity", "mortality"]'::jsonb,0,'Incidence counts new cases.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.E',4,'In a town of 10,000 people, 50 people die from a disease in a year. The mortality rate per 10,000 is:','["0.5", "50", "5", "500"]'::jsonb,1,'50 per 10,000.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.F',3,'A virus that spreads across many countries and continents causes a global health challenge called a:','["picnic", "vacation", "pandemic", "parade"]'::jsonb,2,'Pandemics spread widely.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.F',4,'Antibiotic resistance, climate change, and aging populations are all challenges in global health that can have an impact on how:','["rivers flow", "moons orbit", "people dress", "countries provide care"]'::jsonb,3,'Global challenges affect health systems.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.G',3,'Having reliable access to enough healthy food is called food:','["security", "ownership", "decoration", "variety"]'::jsonb,0,'Food insecurity harms health.','original'),
('127.480.d.1.G',4,'Social determinants of health, like housing, income, and education, affect a person''s health:','["looks", "outcomes", "tastes", "clothes"]'::jsonb,1,'Social conditions shape health.','original'),
('127.480.d.2.A',3,'In developing countries, there are often fewer doctors per person, so the availability of care is:','["higher", "unlimited", "lower", "identical"]'::jsonb,2,'Resources vary.','original'),
('127.480.d.2.A',4,'Compared with developed countries, developing countries often have lower quality health care because of fewer hospitals and:','["restaurants", "tourists", "highways", "medical supplies"]'::jsonb,3,'Supplies and facilities affect quality.','original'),
('127.480.d.2.B',3,'A health care system in which the government pays for care for all citizens through taxes is called a single-payer or national health:','["insurance system", "tourism system", "shipping system", "parade system"]'::jsonb,0,'Government-funded systems.','original'),
('127.480.d.2.B',4,'The four basic models for health systems are the Beveridge, Bismarck, national health insurance, and the:','["trade model", "out-of-pocket model", "gift model", "free-for-all model"]'::jsonb,1,'Out-of-pocket is the fourth model.','original'),
('127.480.d.2.C',3,'Two countries with different systems, such as Canada and the United States, may differ in how health care is paid for and in how much is spent per:','["road", "bus", "person", "tree"]'::jsonb,2,'Systems differ in funding and spending.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_70_v1'
from (values
('127.480.d.2.C',4,'Comparing the life expectancy of countries with different health systems helps researchers learn how systems affect:','["movie ratings", "car sales", "shoe sizes", "health outcomes"]'::jsonb,3,'Outcomes depend on systems.','original'),
('127.480.d.2.D',3,'Over the last decades, the total amount spent on health care in the United States has generally:','["increased", "decreased", "vanished", "stayed zero"]'::jsonb,0,'Spending has grown.','original'),
('127.480.d.2.D',4,'When health expenditures grow faster than the rest of the economy, they take up a larger share of the nation''s:','["population", "gross domestic product", "calendar", "weather"]'::jsonb,1,'GDP share has grown.','original'),
('127.480.d.2.E',3,'New technology, an aging population, and high drug prices are major contributors to the rising:','["size of schools", "speed of trains", "cost of health care", "height of buildings"]'::jsonb,2,'Cost drivers.','original'),
('127.480.d.2.E',4,'Chronic diseases such as diabetes require long-term treatment, which contributes to rising health care:','["luck", "savings", "speed", "spending"]'::jsonb,3,'Chronic disease increases spending.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.A',3,'Technologies that help prevent infection include sterilization, vaccines, and water:','["treatment", "rationing", "scenting", "coloring"]'::jsonb,0,'Water treatment prevents disease.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.A',4,'Rapid diagnostic tests that detect a virus in minutes support the prevention and treatment of infectious disease by allowing early:','["shopping", "isolation and care", "vacations", "sales"]'::jsonb,1,'Quick tests speed response.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.B',3,'A vaccine protects public health by training the immune system and helping create:','["herd gossip", "herd hunger", "herd immunity", "herd shopping"]'::jsonb,2,'Herd immunity protects the community.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.B',4,'When most people in a community are vaccinated, those who cannot be vaccinated are protected indirectly. This is called:','["private immunity", "random immunity", "temporary shelter", "community immunity"]'::jsonb,3,'Community immunity lowers spread.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.C',3,'Taking antibiotics when they are not needed, or not finishing a prescribed course, can lead to:','["antibiotic resistance", "better sleep", "faster growth", "stronger bones"]'::jsonb,0,'Misuse creates resistant bacteria.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.C',4,'Antibiotics work against bacteria but not against viruses, so using them for a cold is an example of:','["vaccination", "misuse", "prevention", "correct use"]'::jsonb,1,'Antibiotics do not treat viruses.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.D',3,'Technologies such as genetic testing can help doctors tailor treatment to a person''s DNA, called personalized:','["fashion", "tourism", "medicine", "music"]'::jsonb,2,'Personalized medicine uses genetics.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.D',4,'Molecular diagnostics, such as PCR tests, find the genetic material of a pathogen, which allows doctors to:','["plan a trip", "paint a wall", "fix a car", "identify an infection"]'::jsonb,3,'PCR detects pathogens.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.E',3,'Imaging such as MRI and CT scans help doctors diagnose and treat conditions by showing the inside of the:','["body", "car", "bank", "school"]'::jsonb,0,'Imaging reveals internal structures.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.E',4,'Radiation therapy and chemotherapy are technologies used in the treatment of:','["colds", "cancer", "sunburn", "hiccups"]'::jsonb,1,'Treatments for cancer.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.F',3,'A machine that does the work of failing kidneys by filtering the blood is a dialysis machine, which supports vital organ:','["speed", "color", "failure", "growth"]'::jsonb,2,'Dialysis replaces kidney function.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.F',4,'Technologies like ventilators, artificial hearts, and organ transplants support patients with vital organ:','["vacations", "growth", "donation fees", "failure"]'::jsonb,3,'These support failing organs.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.G',3,'Seeing a doctor by video call from home is an example of:','["telehealth", "tele-shopping", "tele-travel", "tele-sports"]'::jsonb,0,'Telehealth delivers care remotely.','original'),
('127.480.d.3.G',4,'Wearable devices that send a patient''s heart rate to a doctor are an example of remote patient:','["dining", "monitoring", "shopping", "gaming"]'::jsonb,1,'Remote monitoring is digital health.','original'),
('127.480.d.4.A',3,'In a clinical trial, one group receives the treatment and a control group receives a placebo or standard care. The purpose of the control group is to provide a:','["snack", "gift", "comparison", "rest"]'::jsonb,2,'Controls allow comparison.','original'),
('127.480.d.4.A',4,'In a double-blind clinical trial, neither the participants nor the researchers know who receives the treatment, which reduces:','["accuracy", "participation", "cost to zero", "bias"]'::jsonb,3,'Blinding reduces bias.','original'),
('127.480.d.4.B',3,'A study with 1,000 participants has a larger sample size than a study with 20 participants. A larger sample generally gives more:','["reliable results", "errors", "complaints", "delays"]'::jsonb,0,'Larger samples reduce chance error.','original'),
('127.480.d.4.B',4,'A researcher wants 50 participants in each of 3 groups. The total sample size is:','["100", "150", "53", "47"]'::jsonb,1,'50 x 3 = 150.','original'),
('127.480.d.4.C',3,'Measuring blood pressure in numbers is a quantitative method, while interviewing patients about how they feel is a:','["random method", "secret method", "qualitative method", "quantitative method"]'::jsonb,2,'Qualitative methods describe experiences.','original'),
('127.480.d.4.C',4,'Counting how many patients recover is a quantitative method because it produces:','["opinions only", "pictures only", "stories only", "numerical data"]'::jsonb,3,'Quantitative data are numbers.','original'),
('127.480.d.4.D',3,'The first phase of a pharmaceutical trial tests the safety of a drug in a small group of people. This is Phase:','["one", "four", "two", "three"]'::jsonb,0,'Phase I tests safety.','original'),
('127.480.d.4.D',4,'Phase III trials involve large groups to confirm effectiveness and monitor side effects before a drug can be:','["renamed", "approved", "ignored", "invented"]'::jsonb,1,'Phase III precedes approval.','original'),
('127.480.d.5',3,'Clinical research must follow ethical and legal rules, such as obtaining informed consent from participants before the study begins. Informed consent means that participants:','["are not told the risks", "must join", "voluntarily agree after learning the risks", "are paid to stay silent"]'::jsonb,2,'Consent protects participants.','original'),
('127.480.d.5',4,'An institutional review board reviews research on people to make sure that it is ethical and that participants are:','["secret", "charged", "excluded", "protected"]'::jsonb,3,'IRBs protect participants.','original'),
('127.480.d.6.A',3,'Health science research is funded by sources such as government grants, universities, private foundations, and:','["companies", "lotteries only", "tourists", "weather"]'::jsonb,0,'Funding comes from many sources.','original'),
('127.480.d.6.A',4,'In the United States, a major federal source of money for medical research is the National Institutes of:','["History", "Health", "Hobbies", "Housing"]'::jsonb,1,'NIH funds research.','original'),
('127.480.d.6.B',3,'Before a new drug can be sold in the United States, it must be approved by the:','["Postal Service", "Park Service", "Food and Drug Administration", "Weather Service"]'::jsonb,2,'FDA approves drugs.','original'),
('127.480.d.6.B',4,'The FDA reviews data from clinical trials to decide whether a new drug is safe and:','["famous", "cheap", "colorful", "effective"]'::jsonb,3,'Approval requires safety and effectiveness.','original'),
('127.480.d.6.C',3,'The cost of a new medical technology, rules about approval, and doctors'' willingness to adopt it are factors that affect its:','["spread", "weight", "sound", "color"]'::jsonb,0,'Dissemination depends on many factors.','original'),
('127.480.d.6.C',4,'A new device may be slow to reach rural hospitals because of high prices and a lack of trained staff. These are factors that affect:','["decoration", "dissemination", "weather", "scheduling"]'::jsonb,1,'Dissemination barriers.','original'),
('127.480.d.7.A',3,'At the end of a health science project, students analyze the data and communicate their results clearly using graphs and:','["costumes", "songs", "summaries", "riddles"]'::jsonb,2,'Results are communicated clearly.','original'),
('127.480.d.7.A',4,'Experimental results are easier to understand when shown in a labeled graph with a title and axis:','["jokes", "coupons", "stickers", "labels"]'::jsonb,3,'Labels make graphs clear.','original'),
('127.480.d.7.B',3,'Presenting a project to classmates and health professionals lets students receive:','["feedback", "grades only", "prizes only", "gifts"]'::jsonb,0,'Presentations invite feedback.','original'),
('127.480.d.7.B',4,'When presenting to parents, a student should explain the purpose, methods, results, and conclusion using language they can:','["forget", "understand", "doubt", "avoid"]'::jsonb,1,'Match language to audience.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
